她大概有多大？

145
00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:26.600
She was about the size of an American Girl doll.
她差不多有美利坚女孩娃娃那么大。

146
00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:31.400
Well, it sounded like a precursor to an American Girl doll is what I was going to say.
嗯，我正想说听起来像是美利坚女孩娃娃的前身。

147
00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:32.180
It kind of was.
有点像。

148
00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:33.840
Yeah, I think it was.
对，我想是的。

149
00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:36.740
But this predates the Cabbage Patch Kid.
但这比椰菜娃娃还要早。

150
00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:38.500
That was the craze.
那才是风靡一时。

151
00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:39.000
Yes.
是。

152
00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:42.160
The Cabbage Patch Kid 80s?
是80年代的菜园宝宝吗？

153
00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:43.780
I feel like it was.
我觉得是。

154
00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:47.280
And I was like obsessed with my Cabbage Patch Kid.
而且我当时超级迷恋我的菜园宝宝。

155
00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:47.680
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

156
00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.500
Whose name was Christine.
它的名字叫克里斯蒂娜。

157
00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:50.980
Oh.
哦。

158
00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:52.040
What?
什么？

159
00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:52.820
Yeah.
对。

160
00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:59.460
Christine Marie and Casey Alexander were my two Cabbage Patch children.
克里斯蒂娜·玛丽和凯西·亚历山大是我的两个菜园宝宝。

161
00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:00.940
I loved them.
我很爱他们。

162
00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:02.740
Beautiful girls.
漂亮的女孩。

163
00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:03.400
Yeah.
对。

164
00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:05.840
Well, Judy, thank you so much for that question.
好的，朱迪，非常感谢你提出这个问题。

165
00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:08.820
I think we had a lot to say about our lunchboxes.
我觉得我们对饭盒有很多话要说。

166
00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:10.960
And why don't we take a quick break?
我们为什么不休息一下呢？

167
00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:15.040
And when we come back, Christine, we heard you're a real big fan of The Office.
等我们回来时，克里斯蒂娜，听说你是《办公室》的超级粉丝。

168
00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:17.480
So we can't wait to ask you about that.
所以我们迫不及待地想问你关于这个的事。

169
00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:21.180
But also, you and I have three things in common that are kind of fun.
而且，你和我还有三个挺有意思的共同点。

170
00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:22.360
Ooh.
噢。

171
00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:22.860
Ooh.
噢。

172
00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:24.400
Dun, dun, dun.
当、当、当。

173
00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:25.720
That's a good cliffhanger.
真是个不错的悬念。

174
00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:35.650
All right.
好的。

175
00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:36.490
We are back.
我们回来了。

176
00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:39.310
Christine, are you ready to hear what you and I have in common?
克里斯蒂娜，你准备好听听你和我有什么共同点了吗？

177
00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:40.590
I cannot wait.
我等不及了。

178
00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:40.730
Wait.
等等。

179
00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:43.150
This was really fun for me to find out.
我发现这件事的时候觉得特别有趣。

180
00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.390
Well, first of all, we both love tennis.
首先，我们都喜欢网球。

181
00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:49.650
And we were both at Wimbledon this year, not on the same day.
而且我们今年都在温网现场，虽然不是同一天。

182
00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:50.550
Okay.
好吧。

183
00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:52.650
But we both had tickets to center court.
但我们都买到了中心球场的票。

184
00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:54.350
But you, am I correct?
但是你，我没记错吧？

185
00:08:54.350 --> 00:08:55.690
You were in the royal box.
你在皇家包厢里。

186
00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:56.290
Is that right?
是这样吗？

187
00:08:56.290 --> 00:09:01.070
We did get ourselves into the royal box.
我们确实进了皇家包厢。

188
00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:01.490
Yes.
是的。

189
00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:02.670
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

190
00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:03.710
And I take no responsibility.
我可不居功。

191
00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:06.530
That's a perk of my husband.
那是我丈夫带来的福利。

192
00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:07.310
Yes.
是的。

193
00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:07.710
Yes.
是的。

194
00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:09.210
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

195
00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:13.730
It's so special, the tennis experience.
网球体验真的很特别。

196
00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:14.550
Don't you think?
你不觉得吗？

197
00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:15.150
Yes.
是的。

198
00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:18.410
I've been to the three of the four Grand SlaMs.
四大满贯我去过三个。

199
00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:19.150
Wow.
哇。

200
00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:20.890
Have not been to the Australian Open.
还没去过澳大利亚网球公开赛。

201
00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:24.050
But diehard tennis fan.
但我是一个坚定的网球迷。

202
00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:26.130
Like, grew up watching it.
就那种，从小看到大。

203
00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:27.150
I played a little.
我以前也打一点。

204
00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:28.090
I played okay.
我打得还可以。

205
00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:29.230
I was never great.
从来算不上顶尖。

206
00:09:29.350 --> 00:09:30.970
I played on my high school tennis team.
我曾是高中网球队的成员。

207
00:09:31.790 --> 00:09:32.270
Mediocre.
水平平平。

208
00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:37.970
But the watching it, and from a really young age, but we belonged to like a tennis swim club
但我真的很喜欢看比赛，而且从小就开始看了，我们以前加入过一个网球游泳俱乐部

209
00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:38.550
growing up.
伴随着成长。

210
00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:41.170
I grew up in Pennsylvania, and they'd do a trip to the U.S.
我在宾夕法尼亚州长大，他们会组织去美国

211
00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:43.970
Open, nosebleed seats, but
网开赛，买的都是山顶看台票，但

212
00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:49.450
like we would all bus in, and everyone would just scatter and then meet back at like 10
就像我们所有人坐大巴去，然后大家各自散开，晚上十点

213
00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:50.150
o'clock at night.
左右再集合。

214
00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:58.270
And so my memories of those years were the early 80s of like McEnroe and Becker.
所以我对那些年——也就是八十年代初的记忆，全是麦肯罗和贝克尔这样的人。

215
00:09:58.710 --> 00:10:03.370
I mean, so many of the big sort of icons were playing still back then.
我的意思是，当时有那么多巨星偶像还在打球。

216
00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:04.770
And I just fell in love with it.
我就是深深地爱上了它。

217
00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:06.890
Steffi Graf and Kim Clijsters.
斯蒂芬妮·格拉芙和金·克里斯特尔斯。

218
00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:07.850
Oh, my God.
哦，天哪。

219
00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:08.490
All of them.
全都有。

220
00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:09.170
All of them.
全都有。

221
00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:11.010
Okay, so that's one thing.
好吧，这是第一件事。

222
00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:12.030
Okay, that's tennis.
好，那是网球。

223
00:10:12.370 --> 00:10:16.970
And then my second thing, and this is the thing that just completely floored my family.
然后我的第二件事，这件事简直让我全家人大跌眼镜。

224
00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:20.890
So you're in many movies that are my family's favorites.
你参演了好多我家人最喜欢的电影。

225
00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:23.890
All my kids are so tickled that I'm meeting you today.
我所有的孩子一听说我今天要见你，都高兴坏了。

226
00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:29.710
But as we were going through your filmography, because each night we're on a little mini vacation,
但当我们翻看你的作品年表时，因为我们每晚都在进行一个小小的度假，

227
00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:31.670
we've been watching a movie that you're in.
我们一直在看你演的电影。

228
00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:32.890
Oh, my God.
哦，天哪。

229
00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:34.510
Okay, that's mortifying.
好吧，这太尴尬了。

230
00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:36.570
No, no, it was great.
不，不，这很棒。

231
00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:36.780
Oh, God.
哦，天哪。

232
00:10:36.870 --> 00:10:37.590
It was great.
这太棒了。

233
00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:43.250
But so as we're looking up your filmography, my husband was like, wait a second.
但就在我们查阅你的作品年表时，我丈夫突然说，等等。

234
00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:45.830
We were in a Hallmark Christmas movie together.
我们一起演过一部 Hallmark 圣诞电影。

235
00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:47.690
And I was like, what?
然后我说，什么？

236
00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:48.130
Wait.
等等。

237
00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:51.550
First of all, my kids and I didn't even know my husband was in a Hallmark Christmas movie.
首先，我和孩子们甚至都不知道我丈夫演过 Hallmark 圣诞电影。

238
00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:54.510
It's called Farewell, Mr. Kringle.
片名叫《再见，克林格先生》。

239
00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:56.990
Because that's the only Hallmark movie I did.
因为那是我拍的唯一一部 Hallmark 电影。

240
00:10:57.310 --> 00:10:57.910
Okay.
好吧。

241
00:10:58.110 --> 00:10:59.510
Are you ready for this?
你准备好听这个了吗？

242
00:10:59.710 --> 00:11:03.230
He played your husband who died in the plane crash.
他演了你在飞机失事中去世的丈夫。

243
00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:04.050
Stop.
别开玩笑了。

244
00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:05.090
Yes.
是的。

245
00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:06.830
Who I never met.
我从来没见过他。

246
00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:08.690
No, you had no scenes together.
对，你们没有对手戏。

247
00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:11.810
Shot on another day, like a flashback, right?
是另一天拍的，类似于闪回，对吧？

248
00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:12.290
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

249
00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:13.690
They're all your flashbacks.
全都是关于你的闪回。

250
00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:14.590
But yes.
但确实是的。

251
00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:15.370
No.
没有。

252
00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:17.270
Isn't that crazy?
这不是很疯狂吗？

253
00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:21.530
I have to track down how to watch that.
我得找找怎么看那个。

254
00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:23.470
Is that an easy find or no?
那个容易找到吗？

255
00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:24.530
That's an easy find.
那个很容易找到。

256
00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:31.550
And also, we found the scene where you drift off in thought and then you flashback to him talking to you.
而且，我们找到了你陷入沉思然后闪回他跟你说话的那场戏。

257
00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:37.410
And my kids are just, maybe this is one of their new favorite things that we've ever discovered.
而且我的孩子们，这可能是他们发现的我们最新的最爱之一。

258
00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:39.210
Like, they can't get over it.
简直让他们念念不忘。

259
00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:44.250
It's, you know, I, by the way, that was one of the most fun jobs.
就是，你知道的，我，顺便说一句，那是我最开心的一份工作之一。

260
00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:48.190
Like, doing a Hallmark movie, you know, it's like so dialed in.
就像，拍一部 Hallmark 的电影，你知道，真的是轻车熟路。

261
00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:51.770
And, you know, you shoot like in Santa Clarita or somewhere up there.
而且，你知道，你就在圣克拉里塔或者那附近拍摄。

262
00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:54.830
Oh, I did a Hallmark Christmas movie, was it two years ago?
哦，我拍过一部 Hallmark 的圣诞电影，是两年前吗？

263
00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:57.330
And it's still one of the most fun experiences I've had.
而且它仍然是我有过最有趣的体验之一。

264
00:11:57.430 --> 00:11:58.470
It was so great.
真的太棒了。

265
00:11:58.750 --> 00:11:59.730
Everybody's so nice.
每个人都特别好。

266
00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:02.270
It was just, like, they treat you so well.
就是那种，他们对你太好了。

267
00:12:02.270 --> 00:12:03.250
And it was so great.
而且真的太棒了。

268
00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:08.050
But I don't think I've seen it since it debuted.
但我感觉自从它首播之后我就没看过。

269
00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:10.550
Well, you're very good in it.
好吧，你在里面演得非常好。

270
00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:12.130
Thank you.
谢谢你。

271
00:12:12.470 --> 00:12:17.230
Okay, my last thing is you and I both graduated in the class of 1989.
好的，我的最后一件事是你和我都是1989届毕业的。

272
00:12:17.690 --> 00:12:18.490
Well, hello.
哇，你好啊。

273
00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:19.110
Hello.
你好。

274
00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:20.130
Hello.
你好。

275
00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:21.890
And I told my kids that.
我把这件事告诉了我的孩子们。

276
00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:25.150
And then I told them, I guess this isn't so much a thing anymore.
然后我告诉他们，我想这现在已经不算什么了。

277
00:12:25.150 --> 00:12:28.990
But, like, when we were in high school, every graduating class had their own chant.
但是，就像我们上高中时，每个毕业班都有自己的口号。

278
00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:30.250
Do you remember?
你还记得吗？

279
00:12:30.490 --> 00:12:32.290
Like, ours was, we're so great.
比如我们的是，我们太棒了。

280
00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:33.090
We're so fine.
我们太优秀了。

281
00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:34.350
We're the class of 89.
我们是89届的。

282
00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:38.550
And my kids were like, what?
然后我的孩子们就问，什么？

283
00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:40.610
I wondered if that was a Texas thing.
我在想那是不是德克萨斯州特有的。

284
00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:42.990
Because Angela asked me what my school chant was.
因为安吉拉问我我的学校口号是什么。

285
00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:46.190
And I thought, well, I don't remember having one necessarily.
我想了想，觉得我们好像不一定有这东西。

286
00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.370
I don't either.
我也没有。

287
00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:52.990
And I went to Catholic school in Pennsylvania.
而且我在宾夕法尼亚州上的是天主教学校。

288
00:12:53.030 --> 00:12:56.990
But the tune you just gave, and I wasn't a cheerleader in high school.
但你刚才哼出的调子，我高中时又不是拉拉队员。

289
00:12:57.110 --> 00:13:01.250
But I just remember that same chant is, it's all right.
但我只记得同样的口号是，没关系。

290
00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:01.910
It's okay.
没事的。

291
00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:03.430
We're going to beat them anyway.
反正我们也要打败他们。

292
00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:04.530
Yes.
对。

293
00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:07.230
So it's just whatever words.
所以就是随便填什么词都行。

294
00:13:07.650 --> 00:13:08.090
Exactly.
没错。

295
00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:08.690
I know.
我知道。

296
00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:10.050
We thought we were so cool.
我们当时觉得自己酷毙了。

297
00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:11.250
And we would chant that.
而且我们会齐声喊那个。

298
00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:15.710
Like, at pep rallies, each grade would go and say their grade chant.
就像在动员大会上，每个年级都会去喊他们年级的口号。

299
00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:20.190
And then there were, like, the party girls, like, the kind of wild gals.
然后还有那种派对女孩，就是比较疯狂的女生。

300
00:13:20.430 --> 00:13:20.930
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

301
00:13:20.930 --> 00:13:23.730
And they extended it to, we're so cool.
而且他们把它延伸成了，我们太酷了。

302
00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:24.750
We're so fine.
我们太棒了。

303
00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:26.370
We drink wine.
我们喝红酒。

304
00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:27.930
Or something like that.
或者类似这样的话。

305
00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:29.070
We're the class of 89.
我们是89届的。

306
00:13:29.610 --> 00:13:29.750
Yeah.
是啊。

307
00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:30.170
But, yeah.
不过，对吧。

308
00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:39.190
I feel like even in the world that I was in, which was very different than the John Hughes Breakfast Club world, that was so relatable because of all the cliques.
我觉得即使在我所处的那个世界里，它与约翰·休斯的《早餐俱乐部》那个世界大不相同，但它也非常引人共鸣，因为有很多小集团。

309
00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:40.970
You know, there were the jocks.
你知道，有那些运动员。

310
00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:45.330
But we didn't call them the sportos or the, you know, we didn't call them that.
但我们不叫他们运动迷，你知道，我们不那样叫他们。

311
00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:55.030
But the people that, when you would bus in to the parking lot in the morning and you'd see the kids standing on the street corner smoking, like,
但是那些人，当你早上坐大巴进停车场，看到孩子们站在街角抽烟，就像是，

312
00:13:55.030 --> 00:13:57.430
there were kids that smoked in high school.
有些孩子在高中就抽烟。

313
00:13:57.790 --> 00:13:58.150
Oh, yeah.
噢，是的。

314
00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:00.130
I was not one of them.
